{#
  Case study index — the `caseStudy` single, which owns /case-study. The individual
  studies live in the `caseStudies` structure at /case-study/{slug} and render from
  _views/structure/caseStudies/default.twig.

  NOTE the router keys off the section's NAME, kebab-cased (see _routers/single.twig),
  not its handle — the section is named "Case Studies" and handled `caseStudy`, so this
  directory has to be `case-studies`. Rename the section in the CMS and this directory
  has to be renamed with it, or the page 404s on a LoaderError.

  Same `_components/content` shape as the contact single and a case study page, with
  the grid of cards below. Cards come from `_components/case-study`, the same
  component Jonson surfaces in an answer, so a study looks the same wherever it's met.

  `status('live')` matches FindContext: disabled, future-dated and expired entries
  stay out. Featured first, mirroring the [[casestudies:all]] ordering.
#}
{% extends '_layouts/page.twig' %}

{% set tplPath = _self %}

{# Cream slab, as on the contact page and a case study — the default is olive p500. #}
{% set slabModifier = 'b-slab--l600' %}

{% block siteContent %}
    {% set studies = craft.entries()
        .section('caseStudies')
        .status('live')
        .all() %}

    {# Structure order, straight through — `caseStudies` is a Structure section, so the
       query already comes back in the order the entries are dragged into in the CP.
       That IS the running order for this page: it's the one view that shows every
       study, so the sequence should be whatever you arranged, top to bottom.

       Deliberately NOT featured-first. `isFeatured` is quality control for the places
       that show a SUBSET and have to choose — the Jonson panel picking a few studies
       for a generic question, the strip at the foot of a study. Here nothing is being
       chosen, so promoting the flagged ones only overrides the ordering you set by
       hand with a flag that was answering a different question. #}
    {% set ordered = studies %}

    {# Whisper is set here rather than from entry.title: the single is titled "Case
       Study" (singular), which reads wrong above a list of several — and that title
       is also the browser tab and the admin label, so it's not the right thing to
       rename just for this line. #}
    {# Both come from the entry, same as the contact single: Title is the whisper,
       Long title the h1 (falling back to Title if it's empty). Set them on the
       `caseStudy` single in the CMS.

       The marquee goes THROUGH the content component rather than after it, so it
       sits inside the timeline — the trailing spine and end node (.c-content::after)
       come after the strip instead of the strip hanging below them. #}
    {# All live testimonials, in the same shape FindContext hands the component:
       quote/name/role/company/image. `status('live')` matches everywhere else —
       disabled, future-dated and expired stay out.

       The company comes from `craft.frontend.testimonialCompany`, not the
       `company` field — a quote with a case study linked is named by the study,
       so the client can't read one way here and another on its own page. #}
    {% set quotes = [] %}
    {% for t in craft.entries().section('testimonials').status('live').all() %}
        {% set quote = t.blockquote ?? '' %}
        {% if quote %}
            {% set quotes = quotes|merge([{
                quote: quote,
                name: t.personName ?? '',
                role: t.jobTitle ?? '',
                company: craft.frontend.testimonialCompany(t),
                image: t.profileImage.one() ?? null,
            }]) %}
        {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}

    {# "Brands I have worked with" logo strip, below the quotes. Same source as the contact page and
       the Jonson [[clients]] panel: only clients that actually have a logo asset. #}
    {% set clients = [] %}
    {% for c in craft.entries().section('clientList').status('live').all() %}
        {% set logo = c.logo.one() %}
        {# Same two gates as the contact single and the Jonson panel: needs a logo, and
           the client's Hidden? switch keeps it out. Null-safe, since the switch is
           unset on anything saved before the field existed. #}
        {% if logo and not (c.isHidden ?? false) %}
            {% set clients = clients|merge([{ name: c.title, logo: logo, summary: c.summary ?? '' }]) %}
        {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}

    {% include '_components/content' with {
        whisper: entry.title,
        title: entry.longTitle ?: entry.title,
        caseStudies: ordered,
        testimonials: quotes,
        clients: clients,
    } only %}

    {# Ask bar as a real footer — a SIBLING of .c-content, not a child. The timeline's
       end node is .c-content::after, so anything inside would sit above it; on the
       green pages the conversation footer likewise comes after the trailing dot. Out
       here it also spans the slab without needing negative margins, since the inline
       padding belongs to .c-content. #}
    {% include '_components/ask' only %}
{% endblock %}
